; Two clients show one view of a 300-line buffer: a desktop 20 lines
; high and a phone 10 lines high, each line 20 pixels, each client a
; device of its own. Before a device has measured the view, its client
; draws 200 items each side of where it is placed, and no spacers; a new
; client follows point, as point moved last.
> (define b (buffers:make "long" (lines 300)))
> (define v (views:make b))
> (drawn v desktop)
(1 201 201 () ())
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone))
((new follow 1) (new follow 1))
; The first report makes the device's height map. The client then draws
; whole items two view heights beyond each edge, in pixels by the map,
; trimming those wholly past twice that, and a spacer stands in for the
; rest beside a scroll sizer as high as the map's total.
> (report! desktop v 1 0 #f)
> (drawn v desktop)
(1 81 81 () (6088))
> (report! phone v 1 0 #f)
> (drawn v phone)
(1 41 41 () (6088))
; A report on the way only draws for the client scrolling: the phone is
; not placed, and the view's position stays.
> (report! desktop v 150 0 #f)
> (drawn v desktop)
(110 209 100 (2180) (6088))
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone) (line-of v (views:top v)))
((same follow 1) (same follow 1) 1)
; Once a hand scroll comes to rest, the view's position moves, and every
; other client is placed there once; the client that scrolled is not.
; Point moves to the first line wholly in view, past the scroll margin.
> (report! desktop v 151 5 #t)
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone) (line-of v (views:top v)) (line-of v (views:point v)))
((same follow 154) (new position 151) 151 154)
> (report! desktop v 151 5 #t)
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone))
((same follow 154) (same position 151))
; The phone's report on the placement confirms it, whatever the phone
; measured, so clients of different sizes never place each other.
> (report! phone v 151 5 #f)
> (report! phone v 151 5 #t)
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone) (line-of v (views:top v)))
((same follow 154) (same position 151) 151)
; Each client's run is its own, and the sizer changes only in a screen
; answering a report at rest.
> (list (drawn v desktop) (drawn v phone))
((110 211 102 (2180) (6079)) (131 181 51 (2600) (6088)))
; A report on an older placement than the newest sent to its client is
; ignored, but its number comes back on the client's screen.
> (views:scroll-to! v (line-start v 200) (views:align top))
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone))
((new top 200) (new top 200))
> (define (report-on placement client top)
    ((table-ref web:input-handlers "scroll") client
     `(("type" . "scroll") ("view" . ,(views:id v)) ("placement" . ,placement) ("report" . 99) ("version" . 0)
       ("top" . (("line" . ,top))) ("offset" . 0) ("itemHeight" . 20) ("left" . 0) ("start" . null) ("end" . null)
       ("spacer" . null) ("spacerDistance" . 0) ("below" . 0) ("items" . #()) ("lineHeight" . 20) ("charWidth" . 10)
       ("width" . 800) ("height" . 200) ("settled" . #t) ("hand" . #t) ("runAtEnd" . #f))))
> (report-on (- (car (numbers-after (html-of v phone) "data-placement=\"")) 1) phone 20)
> (list (line-of v (views:top v)) (car (numbers-after (html-of v phone) "data-reported=\"")))
(200 99)
; A fling that outruns what is drawn reports from the spacer above: the
; top is counted across the spacer from the first item drawn, at the
; px the spacer was drawn with, and drawn around.
> (report! desktop v 200 0 #f)
> (drawn v desktop)
(160 259 100 (3180) (6079))
> (report! desktop v 60 7 #f)
> (list (drawn v desktop) (line-of v (views:top v)) (line-of v (views:top v desktop)))
((1 120 120 () (6079)) 200 60)
; The report at rest from the screen drawn there moves the view, and
; point, below what is in view, to the last line wholly in view inside
; the margin.
> (report! desktop v 60 7 #t)
> (list (line-of v (views:top v)) (placement v phone) (line-of v (views:point v)))
(60 (new position 60) 77)
> (report! phone v 60 7 #f)
; A command that moves point sends every client a placement that follows
; point, which each browser applies in its own geometry. The report of
; the client whose command it was makes what it shows the view's
; position; the others keep their own.
> (as-client phone (lambda () (views:set-point! v (line-start v 75))))
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone))
((new follow 75) (new follow 75))
> (report! phone v 68 0 #f)
> (report! desktop v 61 0 #f)
> (list (line-of v (views:top v)) (line-of v (views:top v desktop)) (line-of v (views:top v phone)))
(68 61 68)
> (as-client phone (lambda () (line-of v (views:top v))))
68
> (views:top v 'nobody)
! views:top: not a client or #f with irritant nobody
; C-v moves every client by the commanding client's view height less two
; lines, from what its browser shows, by its device's map, and moves
; point into what that browser then shows.
> (define (run client command) (views:with-view v (as-client client (lambda () (commands:run command)))))
> (run desktop views:scroll-up)
> (list (placement v desktop) (placement v phone))
((new position 79) (new position 79))
> (report! desktop v 79 0 #f)
> (line-of v (views:point v))
81
> (run desktop views:scroll-down)
> (placement v desktop)
(new position 61)
; C-l puts point's place at the centre, then the top, then the bottom;
; the place in text is a mark styled as the cursor, drawn while the
; placement is the newest. Until the browser has measured the newest
; placement, M-v waits for its report.
> (report! desktop v 61 0 #f)
> (as-client desktop (lambda () (views:set-point! v (line-start v 70))))
> (run desktop views:recenter-top-bottom)
> (list (placement v desktop) (and (search (html-of v desktop) "<span class=\"view-place\"></span><span class=\"cursor primary\"></span>line 70" 0) #t))
((new center 70) #t)
> (run desktop views:recenter-top-bottom)
> (placement v desktop)
(new top 70)
> (run desktop views:recenter-top-bottom)
> (placement v desktop)
(new bottom 70)
> (run desktop views:scroll-down)
> (placement v desktop)
(same bottom 70)
> (report! desktop v 51 0 #f)
> (list (placement v desktop) (search (html-of v desktop) "view-place" 0))
((new position 33) #f)
; C-v raises at the end only once the browser shows the run's end with
; nothing below it; M-v raises at the start.
> (report! desktop v 281 0 #f)
> (report! desktop v 282 0 #f)
> (run desktop views:scroll-up)
